Swift packages

  BroadwaveKit (apple/Packages/BroadwaveKit/Package.swift) has no external
  package dependencies. It is part of this repository, Apache-2.0.
  BroadwaveUI (apple/Packages/BroadwaveUI/Package.swift) depends on
  BroadwaveKit by local path. Apache-2.0.
  The iOS and tvOS apps have no Package.swift. apple/project.yml links the
  same two local packages and no remote ones.

ffmpeg

  The published image (deploy/docker/Dockerfile) and the runtime image
  (deploy/docker/Dockerfile.runtime) install the Debian package
  jellyfin-ffmpeg7 from https://repo.jellyfin.org/debian, suite bookworm,
  component main. They do not install Debian's ffmpeg package. The package
  version is not pinned in either Dockerfile.

  On 2026-09-25, apt's candidate in that suite for amd64 and arm64 was
  jellyfin-ffmpeg7 7.1.4-3-bookworm (source package jellyfin-ffmpeg 7.1.4-3).
  Corresponding source, tag v7.1.4-3:

    https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg
    https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg/archive/refs/tags/v7.1.4-3.tar.gz

  debian/rules at that tag configures the build with --enable-gpl and
  --enable-version3, and links GPL libraries including libx264 and libx265.
  That ffmpeg is GPL-3.0-or-later. The same build also links libfdk-aac,
  which the Jellyfin package ships under the FDK AAC license.

  A later image build can install a newer jellyfin-ffmpeg7 from the same
  suite, because the Dockerfiles do not pin it. For a package version
  X.Y.Z-N-bookworm, the source is tag vX.Y.Z-N in the repository above.
  The image carries this offer at /usr/share/doc/broadwave/ffmpeg-source-offer.txt.
  Broadwave is not linked with ffmpeg. The server runs it as a separate program.

  comskip is not installed by the image. If an operator installs it, it runs
  as its own program under the GPL.
